--TEST--
A `#[Core\Query]` parameter declared `?T` needs the default `null`: without a default, or with another default, it is `E0752`, and the help says to write `= null` — `rule:routing/a-query-parameter-is-declared-like-a-capture`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Blog {
    #[Core\Route(path: "/posts", method: Core\Http\Method::Get)]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function list(#[Core\Query] ?uint $p): string {
        return "";
    }

    #[Core\Route(path: "/feed", method: Core\Http\Method::Get)]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function feed(#[Core\Query] ?uint $p = 1): string {
        return "";
    }
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0752]: `uint|null` is not a type `#[Query] $p` can arrive at without the default `null`
  --> case.nvs:5:26
%A
  = help: a query string cannot carry `null`, so a `?` type means the key may be absent. Write `= null` as the default

error[E0752]: `uint|null` is not a type `#[Query] $p` can arrive at without the default `null`
   --> case.nvs:11:26
%A
   = help: a query string cannot carry `null`, so a `?` type means the key may be absent. Write `= null` as the default, or remove the `?`

error: aborting due to 2 errors
